What is Token based and JWT authentication ?
========================================
→Token-based authentication is a method where the server gives a token to the user after successful login.
→The client sends this token with every request to access protected APIs.
→The server does not store session data; it only verifies the token.
How JWT Authentication Works
User logs in
Server creates a JWT using a secret key
JWT is sent to the client
Client sends JWT in every request
Server verifies JWT signature
If valid → access granted
Example : 
const jwt = require("jsonwebtoken");
const token = jwt.sign(
  { userId: user.id, role: user.role },
  process.env.JWT_SECRET,
  { expiresIn: "1h" }
);
Verifying :
jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET
